    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `/embed/{id}` edge handler (Fastly Compute JS) returns \"Video unavailable\" for all embeds, even when the video exists. The root cause is in `fetchVideoMetadata` in `compute-js/src/index.js` — it never extracted the `.imeta.url` or `.imeta.m` fields from the video API response, so `videoUrl` was always `undefined`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Browser testing confirms embed page hits the edge and fetches metadata from funnelcake\n- Logs show `title: Hey Houston!` but no `videoUrl` in the metadata\n- `renderEmbedPage` receives `videoUrl: undefined` and renders the fallback \"Video unavailable\" message\n- `relay.divine.video/api/oEmbed` returns valid oEmbed JSON for the same video ID — the media itself is fine\n\n## Example Embed URL\n\n- https://divine.video/embed/32686986622f6041ba7d30375135b6ae42c6551fa58d1297acf7074c73863b3e",
